{number: 112}
{title: Shall We Gather at the River}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Shall we gather at the river,
Where bright angel feet have [G7] trod,
With its [C] crystal tide forever
Flowing by the [G7] throne of [C] God?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Yes, we'll [F] gather at the [C] river,
The beautiful, the [G7] beautiful river;
Gather with the [C] saints at the [F] river
That [C] flows by the [G7] throne of [C] God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
On the [C] margin of the river,
Washing up its silver [G7] spray,
We will [C] walk and worship ever,
All the [G7] happy golden [C] day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Soon we'll [C] reach the shining river,
Soon our pilgrimage will [G7] cease;
Soon our [C] happy hearts will quiver
With the [G7] melody of [C] peace.
{end_of_verse}
